  "body": "**Blocked by:** #169, #88\n\n## Context\n\nThis issue builds on #169; #171 is the next sequential slice of the `observability` batch.\n\n## Task\n\nAdd authenticated read-only `GET /api/system-health` aggregating current process freshness/version/uptime, alerting checks, pending/overdue/permanent queue counts, item_automation errors per database, agent-run errors over seven days, and mailbox activity/error. Persist no samples. Add an i18n System status block beside AI usage with healthy, degraded, empty, loading, and request-error states and no content/secrets.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Task deliverables, migrations, integration, automated tests, and necessary documentation.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- No metrics stack, /metrics, or historical time series.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The response contains every specified source.\n- The UI distinguishes all states and identifies degraded components.\n- Czech and English labels use i18n.\n- No metric samples are written.\n",
